inhalt.text:
The class votes on whether to redesign the classroom. {{1}}
The elected school council decides on the theme for the school fair. {{2}}
Young people collect signatures for a cycle path and submit the petition. {{3}}
At a meeting, all club members vote directly on the club’s new constitution. {{4}}
The class elects two delegates to represent its concerns on the school council. {{5}}
A group demonstrates peacefully for more youth spaces in the local area. {{6}}
All eligible voters decide directly on a proposal at the ballot box. {{7}}
The elected parliament debates and passes a new law. {{8}}
Young people use the youth parliament to raise their concerns with the local authority. {{9}}
